**2. Independent Analysis of the Image**

The image, titled "Nano-11 facilitates the transport of antigens to lymph nodes," consists of three panels. Panel A presents flow cytometry plots comparing Alexa Fluor 647-labeled OVA-positive cells and their phenotyping (CD11c vs MHCII) in draining lymph nodes on Day 1 and 2, after immunization with soluble OVA, OVA+aluminum hydroxide (AH), or OVA+Nano-11. Panel B is a bar graph quantifying the mean fluorescence intensity (MFI) of OVA in OVA-containing cells, showing significantly higher MFI for OVA+Nano-11. Panel C, also a bar graph, depicts the percentage of migratory dendritic cells (MigDCs) among OVA-positive cells, indicating adjuvants increase this percentage.

