**3. Relevance of the Image to the PDF Research**

The image is highly relevant to the PDF's research. It directly supports key claims regarding Nano-11's mechanism as a vaccine adjuvant, specifically its ability to enhance antigen delivery and targeting to antigen-presenting cells in vivo. Figure 5 visually demonstrates that Nano-11 leads to a greater number of antigen-positive cells and a significantly higher antigen load per cell (MFI) in the draining lymph nodes compared to soluble antigen or antigen with aluminum adjuvant. This evidence reinforces the papers' conclusions that Nano-11 efficiently targets and delivers antigens to immunopotentiating migratory dendritic cells, contributing to its strong adjuvant effect and desired in vivo kinetics.